255 {"cash": 313, "action": {"action": "propose_trade", "args": {"offer": {"cash": 0, "get_out_of_jail_cards": 0, "properties": ["VIRGINIA_AVENUE"]}, "request": {"cash": 150, "get_out_of_jail_cards": 0, "properties": ["PENNSYLVANIA_AVENUE"]}, "to_player_id": "p2"}, "decision_id": "campaign-c0761df29478459ab4cea725626ea259-6-f3049e5157-dec-000255", "private_thought": "Need a stronger rent engine to compete with dark blues. This completes both sets, with $150 supporting green redemption/development; Virginia is unmortgaged while Pennsylvania is mortgaged. Can finance green houses with spare-property mortgages if accepted.", "public_message": "Virginia completes your pinks. Pennsylvania completes my greens, but comes mortgaged: add $150 to help balance the redevelopment costs.", "schema_version": "v1"}, "events": []}
256 {"cash": 985, "action": {"action": "reject_trade", "args": {}, "decision_id": "campaign-c0761df29478459ab4cea725626ea259-6-f3049e5157-dec-000256", "private_thought": "Only p4 left. Offer is a lie: I have States but not St. Charles, so Virginia does not complete pinks. PA plus their NC and Pacific is a green monopoly. Giving PA even mortgaged plus $150 arms the only set that can kill me. PA is a blocker; never trade it. Their cash is $313; full liquidation about $1543–$1593. BW 4-house rent $1700 already bankrupts them. No safe counter gives them PA, and they will not take one that doesn't. Reject.", "public_message": "No. Virginia doesn't complete the pinks — you still have St. Charles. Pennsylvania completes your greens. Not trading it.", "schema_version": "v1"}, "events": []}
257 {"cash": 313, "action": {"action": "propose_trade", "args": {"offer": {"cash": 0, "get_out_of_jail_cards": 0, "properties": ["ST_CHARLES_PLACE", "VIRGINIA_AVENUE"]}, "request": {"cash": 250, "get_out_of_jail_cards": 0, "properties": ["PENNSYLVANIA_AVENUE"]}, "to_player_id": "p2"}, "decision_id": "campaign-c0761df29478459ab4cea725626ea259-6-f3049e5157-dec-000257", "private_thought": "Correct prior mistake. Both pinks genuinely complete their set; $250 supports green redemption and development. Need a stronger rent engine to have a realistic chance against dark blues; can mortgage isolated assets to fund greens.", "public_message": "You're right—I missed St. Charles. Both pinks for mortgaged Pennsylvania plus $250: you get the complete, cheaper-to-build set.", "schema_version": "v1"}, "events": []}
258 {"cash": 985, "action": {"action": "reject_trade", "args": {}, "decision_id": "campaign-c0761df29478459ab4cea725626ea259-6-f3049e5157-dec-000258", "private_thought": "Only p4 left. St. Charles + Virginia would complete my pinks (I have States), but both pinks are weak vs the kill I already have: PP hotel $1500, BW 4-house $1700. Giving mortgaged PA completes their greens (Pacific+NC+PA) and $250 funds houses. Their liquidation is ~$1553, so BW $1700 already bankrupts them; PP is close. Never trade PA, Ventnor, or States. No safe counter they would take. Reject.", "public_message": "No. Pennsylvania completes your greens. I'm not handing you that set, with or without the pinks.", "schema_version": "v1"}, "events": []}
